lisa-design:
- Contract-first PR (P1 phase 1.3): the server stubs (createEnrollment, listEnrollments, deleteEnrollment answering 501 not-implemented; an admin's deregisterAgent answering 501) are forced by the spec and intended, not a FACTORY-CONTRACT-001 violation. Minting, storing and checking enrollment/refresh tokens and `factory agent enroll` are P1 phase 6.
- registerAgent keeps the `registration` access; the middleware refuses a request carrying X-Factory-Enrollment-Token or X-Factory-Agent-Refresh-Token with 401 "enrollment is not available yet" before the join/owner check, even when the join and owner tokens are also present: an unverifiable credential must not be silently ignored.
- deregisterAgent gets a new `agentOrAdmin` access: an `agt_` bearer goes to a.Agent (unchanged self path, 403 not-your-agent for another agent); anything else goes through the admin check (UI maintainers or CLI token). The handler answers any admin (KindUser or KindCLI) with 501 until phase 6, since an admin delete must also revoke the refresh token, which doesn't exist yet.
- Prefixes: enr_ (enrollment token), arf_ (refresh token), enl_ (Enrollment id), checked free with `git grep` (no hit; existing: agt_, tsk_, run_, wi_, lse_, ses_, eff_, and rtk_ from #101).
- Enrollment.id pattern is the spec's `^enl_[a-z0-9]{26}$` (a lowercase ULID). Code ids today are hex hashes; the examples' uppercase ULIDs are illustrative only. Kept as specified.
- Enrollment.usedAt and .agent are required + nullable (always present, null while unused), like Agent.status.throttledUntil.
- EnrollmentRequest.ttl is an inline string with x-go-type v1alpha1.Duration and `default: 7d` (a $ref to Duration can't carry a default in OpenAPI 3.0). The 30d cap is documented; the server enforces it in phase 6.
- 501 problems keep the existing errorHandler rule (5xx detail not returned, logged at error): clients key on code `not-implemented`. Not changed in a contract PR.
- No 501 response is declared in the spec: it's temporary and the `default` problem response covers it; each description says "until P1 phase 6 ... 501".
- TestContract marks the three enrollment ops as covered by checking the 501 problem (sh.check with 501), so the coverage check still holds for every spec operation.
- The registerAgent example stays the join/owner flow (no refreshToken): it's what the server returns today.
- The admin 403 message "commands need the maintainers Group" is left as is: web mocks mirror the text and web/ can't change in a Go PR.
